  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/1062720b-31ff-4bb3-aac3-ddb4061092c0.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 200px;\" /></p><p>When an object is placed in front of a plane mirror, object distance is equal to the image distance. In the first case, the image distance will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>&nbsp;from the mirror. In the next case, as the mirror is moved towards the object, the object distance becomes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. Hence, image distance will also be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>.</p></blockquote>",
